# prompts.log

Purpose:
Record human prompts/instructions sent to the agent after the hidden task release.

Use this whenever a human gives the agent a new instruction, changes the prompt, asks it to retry, narrows scope, or redirects its strategy.

Format:

[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] USER_PROMPT
Prompt:
Context:
Expected agent action:

Examples:

[2026-05-21 20:12] USER_PROMPT
Prompt: Read secret_spec/SECRET_SPEC.md fully and create an implementation plan. Do not write code yet.
Context: Hidden task was just released. We want the agent to plan before editing files.
Expected agent action: Produce a phased implementation plan and identify required commands/output format.

[2026-05-21 21:03] USER_PROMPT
Prompt: Focus only on failing public tests in level_03. Do not rewrite the whole solution.
Context: Public score: 94/250. Main failing category: bracket parsing.
Expected agent action: Inspect failures, patch only relevant parser code, rerun tests.

[2026-05-21 23:40] USER_PROMPT
Prompt: Generate three additional self-tests based on the hidden specification section about exit codes.
Context: Public tests pass for basic cases, but CLI behavior is fragile.
Expected agent action: Create self-tests, run them, patch if needed.

